<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:title "OpenEPCIS Assessment and Test Vocabulary"@en;
    dcterms:description "How a Digital Product Passport states what was measured, tested or assessed about a\nproduct: the assessment that was carried out, the method and the standard that define it, the\nconditions and protocol settings it ran under, the results it produced, the criteria and\nthresholds a result is judged against, and the indicators (scores, classes, expected lifetimes)\nderived from those results.\n\nThe model follows the assessment pattern of the CIRPASS-2 EU DPP ontologies (textile-assessment,\ntextile-indicator): an assessment execution produces results; a result carries a measured value\nwith its unit and names the performance parameter it observes; an indicator is derived from\nresults and is never the result itself. Values with a unit are gs1:QuantitativeValue\n(UN/CEFACT Rec 20 unitCode), so they read the same way as every other quantity in a passport.\n\nThe module sits below the DPP core: it imports only the GS1 Web Vocabulary, schema.org and\nCCCEV, and oec: (dpp-core) imports it. Sector modules add their own performance parameters,\nindicator kinds, test methods, standards and criteria as individuals of the classes here\n(eutex:AbrasionResistance a oea:PerformanceParameter, eutex:MartindaleAbrasionTest a\noea:TestMethod), not new classes.\n\nEPCIS binding: an assessment carried out on an item is an ObjectEvent with action OBSERVE and\nbizStep inspecting. The event is the execution: eventTime, readPoint, bizLocation and the\nsource party say when, where and by whom; the oea:Assessment object hangs at event level under\noea:hasAssessment and carries method, conditions, settings and results. An equivalent compact\nform uses the EPCIS sensorElementList: sensorMetadata.dataProcessingMethod names the method,\nsensorMetadata.bizRules the standard, and each sensorReport carries one result with type set to\nthe oea:PerformanceParameter IRI, value and uom. See docs/EPCIS_BINDING.md.\n\nEPCIS 2.0 Extension:\nThis vocabulary is a first-class EPCIS 2.0 extension per Section 12.3. Declare it using:\n  GS1-Extensions: oea=https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/\n\nReferences:\n- Regulation (EU) 2024/1781 (ESPR), Article 7 and Annex I (performance and information requirements)\n- ISO/IEC 17025:2017, General requirements for the competence of testing and calibration laboratories\n- CIRPASS-2 EU DPP ontologies, textile-assessment and textile-indicator modules\n- SEMICeu Core Criterion and Core Evidence Vocabulary (CCCEV) 2.1"@en;
    dcterms:creator "OpenEPCIS";
    dcterms:license <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0>;
    dcterms:created "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:modified "2026-10-31"^^xsd:date;
    owl:versionInfo "0.9.9";
    owl:versionIRI <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/0.9.9>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "oea";
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/";
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>, <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>, <https://cirpass-2.github.io/ontologies-docs/>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso schema:Observation;
    rdfs:subClassOf schema:Observation;
    rdfs:label "Assessment"@en;
    rdfs:comment "One concrete assessment of a product: a method applied to a specified product under stated conditions and protocol settings, producing results. An assessment made of several tests (a composite durability or recyclability scheme) lists them under oea:hasSubAssessment. When the assessment is reported in an EPCIS event, the event is the execution and supplies time, place and party."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Execution of an assessment method on a product. schema:Observation records an observed value but has no method, condition, protocol setting or criterion; GS1 Web Vocabulary has none of these. Follows the CIRPASS-2 AssessmentExecution pattern."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#AssessmentExecution>;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#DurabilityAssessment>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecyclabilityAssessment>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecycledContentAssessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/TestExecution> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>;
    rdfs:label "Test Execution"@en;
    rdfs:comment "An assessment that performs a test method under controlled test conditions, typically in a laboratory per ISO/IEC 17025."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Laboratory test as a kind of assessment. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#TestExecution>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentMethod> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso schema:measurementMethod;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Method"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A documented procedure for assessing, testing, measuring or scoring a product. Methods are published once as individuals (eutex:MartindaleAbrasionTest, a JRC scoring method) and referenced by every assessment that applies them."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Reusable method definition. schema:measurementMethod and schema:measurementTechnique point at a method but define no class for it; no GS1 or SEMICeu equivalent."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#TestMethod>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecyclabilityScoringMethod>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecyclabilityAssessmentMethod>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#RobustnessScoringMethod>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecycledContentVerificationMethod>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#AgeingSimulationMethod>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/TestMethod> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentMethod>;
    rdfs:label "Test Method"@en;
    rdfs:comment "An assessment method that applies a controlled experimental or inspection procedure, usually defined by a test standard."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Laboratory or inspection method. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#AgeingSimulationMethod>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentStandard> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:referencedFile;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Standard"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A normative or reference document that defines or constrains assessment methods, conditions or result interpretation: an ISO, EN, IEC or OECD standard, a harmonised standard, or a regulatory methodology such as a JRC preparatory study."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Reference document for a method. GS1 Web Vocabulary references documents only as files (gs1:referencedFile); schema.org has no standard class."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#AssessmentStandard>;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#TestingStandard>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentCondition> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Condition"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A condition under which an assessment was performed or a result obtained: a specimen type, a pre-treatment, an environment, a use scenario. Stated as a condition type plus a coded value, a quantity, or a description."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Test condition record. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#AssessmentCondition>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ParameterSetting> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:label "Parameter Setting"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The value a protocol parameter was set to in an assessment: 5 cleaning cycles, 40 °C, 12 kPa. A protocol parameter configures the test; it is not the product property the test observes."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Test protocol setting. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#MeasurementParameterSetting>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentResult> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso schema:Observation;
    rdfs:subClassOf schema:Observation;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Result"@en;
    rdfs:comment "An output of an assessment: a measured value, a rating, an outcome against a criterion, or a textual finding, for one performance parameter."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Result of one assessment. schema:Observation carries a value but no criterion or outcome; no GS1 equivalent."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecyclingYieldResult>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecyclabilityCriterionResult>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementResult> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentResult>;
    rdfs:label "Measurement Result"@en;
    rdfs:comment "An assessment result that records a quantitative value with its unit, or a grade on the scale the method defines (a 1-5 grey-scale rating has unitCode C62)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Quantitative test result. In an EPCIS event the same result can travel as a sensorReport (type, value, uom); see docs/EPCIS_BINDING.md."@en;
    skos:broadMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#AssessmentResult>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/CriterionResult> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentResult>;
    rdfs:label "Criterion Result"@en;
    rdfs:comment "An assessment result that records whether one criterion is met, and the points a scoring method awards for it, without a measured value of its own."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Per-criterion outcome of a scoring scheme (sorting factors of a recyclability score, repair criteria of a repairability index). No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Criterion> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Criterion>;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Criterion"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A criterion a result or an assessment is judged against: a design rule, a requirement of a scoring method, a pass condition. Published once as an individual and referenced by every result that evaluates it."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Specialises cccev:Criterion for product assessments, so criteria authored here read as CCCEV criteria for public-sector consumers."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Threshold> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Constraint>;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Criterion>;
    rdfs:label "Threshold"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A criterion stated as a limit value: a performance parameter, a comparison operator and a quantity (elastane content at most 15 %, biodegradation at least 60 % in 28 days)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Quantitative criterion. CCCEV models limits as cccev:Constraint without operator or parameter."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecycledContentPerformanceThreshold>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso schema:Rating;
    rdfs:subClassOf schema:Observation;
    rdfs:label "Indicator"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A value derived from assessment results to interpret, aggregate or communicate them: a score, a class, an expected lifetime, a number of use cycles. An indicator names its kind, carries a quantity or a coded value, and points at the results and the method it was derived with. It is not a measured value."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Derived score or class. schema:Rating covers review ratings, not method-bound product indicators; no GS1 equivalent."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#LifetimeIndicator>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#DurabilityIndicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/PerformanceParameter> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept;
    rdfs:label "Performance Parameter"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A product characteristic an assessment observes: abrasion resistance, dimensional stability, biodegradation, recyclability rate. Individuals, not classes; sector modules add their own."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Value space for the observed characteristic. CIRPASS-2 models each parameter as a class (textile-durability ObservedPerformanceParameter); here they are concepts, which is how a passport references them."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementParameter> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept;
    rdfs:label "Measurement Parameter"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A protocol parameter a test is configured with: number of cycles, temperature, duration, load, relative humidity. Distinct from the performance parameter the test observes."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Value space for protocol parameters. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#MeasurementParameter>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ConditionType> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept;
    rdfs:label "Condition Type"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The kind of an assessment condition: specimen type, pre-treatment, use scenario. Sector modules add their own."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Value space for condition kinds. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept;
    rdfs:label "Indicator Kind"@en;
    rdfs:comment "What an indicator expresses: a recyclability score, a repairability score, an expected lifetime, a durability class. Sector modules add their own."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Value space for indicator kinds. CIRPASS-2 models each kind as an Indicator subclass; here they are concepts."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Outcome> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept;
    rdfs:label "Outcome"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Whether a result or an assessment meets the criterion it is judged against."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Closed outcome list. CBV dispositions conformant/non_conformant state the same for an item in an event, not for a criterion."@en;
    owl:oneOf _:b0.
_:b0 rdf:first <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Satisfied>;
    rdf:rest _:b1.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Satisfied> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Outcome>;
    rdfs:label "Satisfied"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The result or assessment meets the criterion."@en;
    skos:notation "satisfied".
_:b1 rdf:first <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/NotSatisfied>;
    rdf:rest _:b2.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/NotSatisfied> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Outcome>;
    rdfs:label "Not Satisfied"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The result or assessment does not meet the criterion."@en;
    skos:notation "not_satisfied".
_:b2 rdf:first <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/NotAssessed>;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/NotAssessed> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Outcome>;
    rdfs:label "Not Assessed"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The criterion was not evaluated, for example because it does not apply to the product."@en;
    skos:notation "not_assessed".
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ComparisonOperator> a owl:Class;
    rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept;
    rdfs:label "Comparison Operator"@en;
    rdfs:comment "How a threshold compares a value with its limit."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Closed operator list. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    owl:oneOf _:b3.
_:b3 rdf:first <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/LessThan>;
    rdf:rest _:b4.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/LessThan> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ComparisonOperator>;
    rdfs:label "Less Than"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The value must be below the limit."@en;
    skos:notation "lt".
_:b4 rdf:first <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/LessThanOrEqual>;
    rdf:rest _:b5.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/LessThanOrEqual> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ComparisonOperator>;
    rdfs:label "Less Than or Equal"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The value must not exceed the limit."@en;
    skos:notation "le".
_:b5 rdf:first <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Equal>;
    rdf:rest _:b6.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Equal> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ComparisonOperator>;
    rdfs:label "Equal"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The value must equal the limit."@en;
    skos:notation "eq".
_:b6 rdf:first <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/GreaterThanOrEqual>;
    rdf:rest _:b7.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/GreaterThanOrEqual> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ComparisonOperator>;
    rdfs:label "Greater Than or Equal"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The value must reach at least the limit."@en;
    skos:notation "ge".
_:b7 rdf:first <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/GreaterThan>;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/GreaterThan> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ComparisonOperator>;
    rdfs:label "Greater Than"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The value must be above the limit."@en;
    skos:notation "gt".
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/NumberOfCycles> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementParameter>;
    rdfs:label "Number of Cycles"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Number of repeated test, cleaning, abrasion or simulated-use cycles applied before or during a test (unitCode C62)."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Temperature> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementParameter>;
    rdfs:label "Temperature"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Test temperature (unitCode CEL)."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Duration> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementParameter>;
    rdfs:label "Duration"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Test duration (unitCode DAY, HUR or MIN)."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/RelativeHumidity> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementParameter>;
    rdfs:label "Relative Humidity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Relative humidity of the test atmosphere (unitCode P1)."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Load> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementParameter>;
    rdfs:label "Load"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Mechanical load or pressure applied by the test (unitCode NEW or KPA)."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/RecyclabilityRate> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/PerformanceParameter>;
    rdfs:label "Recyclability Rate"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Mass fraction of the product that can be recycled (unitCode P1, or C62 for a 0-1 fraction). Replaces oec:recyclabilityRate."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/RecoverableRate> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/PerformanceParameter>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#RecoverableRate>;
    rdfs:label "Recoverable Rate"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Mass fraction of the product recoverable at end of life through any recovery operation: material recycling, energy recovery, backfilling (Waste Framework Directive Art. 3(15)). Replaces oec:recoverableRate."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/RecyclingCollectionRate> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/PerformanceParameter>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#RecyclingCollectionRate>;
    rdfs:label "Recycling Collection Rate"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Fraction of products of this type actually collected for recycling under the applicable collection scheme. Replaces oec:recyclingCollectionRate."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/RecyclabilityScore> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind>;
    rdfs:label "Recyclability Score"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Method-specific recyclability score (a JRC textile 0-10 score, a PPWR percentage). A score does not by itself prove that the product will be collected or recycled. Replaces oec:recyclabilityScore."@en;
    skos:closeMatch <https://dpp-keystone.org/spec/v3/terms#recyclabilityScore>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/RepairabilityScore> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind>;
    rdfs:label "Repairability Score"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Method-specific repairability score (French Indice de Réparabilité, EU repairability index; typically 0-10). Replaces oec:repairabilityScore."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/RepairabilityClass> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind>;
    rdfs:label "Repairability Class"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Repairability class band (A to E, A most repairable). Replaces oec:repairabilityClass."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/PerformanceClass> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://dpp-keystone.org/spec/v3/terms#energyEfficiencyClass>;
    rdfs:label "Performance Class"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Performance or efficiency class band (A to G energy-label style). Replaces oec:performanceClass."@en;
    skos:broadMatch <https://dpp-keystone.org/spec/v3/terms#performance>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ExpectedLifetime> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind>;
    rdfs:label "Expected Lifetime"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Lifetime the product is expected to reach under normal use (unitCode ANN). An estimate, not a measured property: it names its method and assumptions. Replaces oec:hasExpectedLifespan."@en;
    skos:closeMatch <urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.Performance:1.2.1#expectedLifetime>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/TechnicalLifetime> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.Performance:1.2.1#batteryTechnicalProperties>;
    rdfs:label "Technical Lifetime"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Lifetime under the conditions stated in the indicator's assessment (unitCode ANN). Replaces oec:hasTechnicalLifetime."@en.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/NumberOfUseCycles> a <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind>;
    rdfs:label "Number of Use Cycles"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Number of use, wash or charge cycles the product is expected to withstand (unitCode C62). A use indicator, not the protocol parameter oea:NumberOfCycles. Replaces oec:usageCycles."@en;
    skos:closeMatch <urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.Performance:1.2.1#expectedNumberOfCycles>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/battery-performance#expectedLifetimeCycles>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasAssessment> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso schema:hasMeasurement;
    rdfs:label "Assessment"@en;
    rdfs:comment "An assessment of the product, from the product master data or from an EPCIS OBSERVE event at event level."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Entry point to an assessment. No domain: it hangs on a gs1:Product, on an EPCIS event, or on a sector container. No GS1 equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasSubAssessment> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso dcterms:hasPart;
    rdfs:label "Sub-Assessment"@en;
    rdfs:comment "An assessment that is part of this one: the spirality, dimensional change and visual inspection tests of a composite robustness assessment."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Composite assessment structure. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasMethod> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso schema:measurementMethod;
    rdfs:label "Method"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The method the assessment applied."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Method of an assessment. schema:measurementMethod is the nearest term and takes free text or a URL."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#appliesMethod>;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentMethod>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasAssessedParameter> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Assessed Parameter"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A performance parameter the assessment targets. Optional: each result names the parameter it observes."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Scope of an assessment. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/PerformanceParameter>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasCondition> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Condition"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A condition the assessment was performed under."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Test condition. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#hasCondition>;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentCondition>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasParameterSetting> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Parameter Setting"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A protocol parameter value the assessment was configured with."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Test protocol setting. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ParameterSetting>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasResult> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Result"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A result the assessment produced."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Output of an assessment. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentResult>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/assessmentDate> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso schema:observationDate;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Date"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Date the assessment was performed. Only for assessments stated in master data; in an EPCIS event the eventTime says when."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Date of an assessment outside an event. schema:observationDate is a dateTime on schema:Observation."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:date;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasAssessmentBody> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Assessment Body"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The laboratory, conformity assessment body or organisation that performed the assessment. In an EPCIS event the source party can say the same."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Performer of an assessment, identified like any GS1 party (GLN)."@en;
    rdfs:range gs1:Organization;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasEvidence> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Evidence>;
    rdfs:label "Evidence"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A document substantiating the assessment: a test report, a certificate, a calculation sheet."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Evidence document, carried as a GS1 referenced file. CCCEV models evidence as cccev:Evidence."@en;
    rdfs:range gs1:ReferencedFileDetails;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasOutcome> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Outcome"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Whether the result, criterion result or whole assessment meets its criterion. On an assessment it states the overall verdict of the method (recyclable, passes ultimate biodegradability)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Pass/fail verdict. No domain: results and assessments both carry one."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Outcome>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/awardedScore> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Awarded Score"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Points a scoring method awards to this result or sub-assessment (spirality 0-3 points of a robustness score, 1 point per sorting factor met)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Component points of a composite score. No domain: results and sub-assessments both carry them."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/isDefinedByStandard> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Defined By Standard"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A standard that defines or constrains the method."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Method-to-standard link. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#isDefinedByStandard>;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentStandard>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentMethod>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/methodUrl> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Method URL"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Where the method is published, for a method stated inline rather than as a named individual."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Method reference. schema:measurementMethod accepts a URL in the same role."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentMethod>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/standardCode> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Standard Code"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Designation of the standard, e.g. ISO 12947-2:2016."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Standard designation. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:string;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentStandard>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/standardUrl> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Standard URL"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Catalogue page of the standard (iso.org, cen.eu, an ELI for a regulation)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Standard reference. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentStandard>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasConditionType> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Condition Type"@en;
    rdfs:comment "What kind of condition this is."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Condition kind. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ConditionType>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentCondition>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasConditionConcept> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Condition Value"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The coded value of the condition, an individual of the sector module's own list (eutex:WovenNonDenim for a specimen-type condition)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Coded condition value. No range: any module's code list may supply it."@en;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentCondition>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasConditionValue> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Condition Quantity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The quantity of the condition, when it is a quantity."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Quantitative condition value."@en;
    rdfs:range gs1:QuantitativeValue;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentCondition>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/conditionDescription> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Condition Description"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Free-text description of the condition, when it is neither coded nor a quantity."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Textual condition. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:string;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentCondition>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasParameter> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Parameter"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The protocol parameter this setting assigns."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Protocol parameter of a setting. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#settingForParameter>;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementParameter>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ParameterSetting>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasParameterValue> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Parameter Value"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The value the protocol parameter was set to."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Protocol parameter value."@en;
    rdfs:range gs1:QuantitativeValue;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ParameterSetting>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasObservedParameter> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Observed Parameter"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The performance parameter this result observes."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "What a result is about. In the EPCIS sensorReport form the same IRI is the report type."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/PerformanceParameter>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentResult>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasMeasuredValue> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso schema:value;
    rdfs:label "Measured Value"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The value obtained, with its UN/CEFACT unit. A grade on the scale the method defines takes unitCode C62."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Measured quantity. In the EPCIS sensorReport form: value and uom."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-assessment#hasMeasuredValue>;
    rdfs:range gs1:QuantitativeValue;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/MeasurementResult>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/resultText> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Result Text"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A finding stated as text, when the result is neither a quantity nor a coded outcome."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://www.iso.org/standard/66912.html>;
    skos:note "Textual result. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:string;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentResult>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/isEvaluatedAgainst> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Evaluated Against"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A criterion or threshold the result, indicator or assessment was judged against; oea:hasOutcome says whether it was met."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Result-to-criterion link. No domain: results, indicators and assessments are judged alike."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Criterion>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasCriterion> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Criterion"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The criterion this criterion result reports on."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Criterion of a criterion result."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Criterion>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/CriterionResult>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/criterionDescription> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Criterion Description"@en;
    rdfs:comment "What the criterion requires, in words."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Criterion text. cccev:Criterion carries the same as dcterms:description."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:string;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Criterion>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/maxScore> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Maximum Score"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The most points a scoring method can award for this criterion."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Weight of a criterion in a composite score. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Criterion>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasThresholdParameter> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Threshold Parameter"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The performance parameter the threshold limits."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Parameter of a limit value."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/PerformanceParameter>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Threshold>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasComparisonOperator> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Comparison Operator"@en;
    rdfs:comment "How the value is compared with the limit."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Operator of a limit value."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/ComparisonOperator>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Threshold>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasThresholdValue> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Threshold Value"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The limit quantity."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://semiceu.github.io/CCCEV/releases/2.1.0/>;
    skos:note "Limit of a threshold."@en;
    rdfs:range gs1:QuantitativeValue;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Threshold>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasIndicator> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Indicator"@en;
    rdfs:comment "An indicator stated for the product or derived by an assessment."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Entry point to an indicator. No domain: it hangs on a gs1:Product, an assessment, or a sector container."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasIndicatorKind> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Indicator Kind"@en;
    rdfs:comment "What the indicator expresses."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Kind of an indicator."@en;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/IndicatorKind>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasIndicatorValue> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Indicator Value"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The indicator as a quantity: a score (unitCode C62), a lifetime (ANN), a number of cycles (C62)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Quantitative indicator value."@en;
    rdfs:range gs1:QuantitativeValue;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasCategoricalValue> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Categorical Value"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The indicator as a coded value from a module's list: a durability class, a shedding risk level, a recyclability grade."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Coded indicator value. No range: any module's code list may supply it."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#hasCategoricalValue>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/indicatorText> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Indicator Text"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The indicator as text, for a class band that has no published code list (a repairability class 'B')."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Uncoded indicator value. Prefer oea:hasCategoricalValue where a code list exists."@en;
    rdfs:range xsd:string;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/isDerivedFrom> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso dcterms:source;
    rdfs:label "Derived From"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A result, assessment or indicator this indicator was calculated from."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Provenance of an indicator. No range: results, assessments and indicators all qualify."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#derivedFrom>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/hasDerivationMethod> a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Derivation Method"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The method the indicator was calculated with (a scoring method, a lifetime estimation method)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Method of an indicator."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#derivedUsingMethod>;
    rdfs:range <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/AssessmentMethod>;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/calculationDescription> a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Calculation Description"@en;
    rdfs:comment "How the indicator was calculated and on which assumptions, when no published method covers it."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Assumptions of an indicator. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#calculationDescription>;
    rdfs:range xsd:string;
    rdfs:domain <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Indicator>.
<https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/> a owl:Ontology;
    dcterms:title "OpenEPCIS DPP Core Vocabulary"@en;
    dcterms:description "Core vocabulary for Digital Product Passports aligned with the EU Ecodesign\nfor Sustainable Products Regulation (ESPR) EU 2024/1781 and GS1 DPP Standards.\n\nOpenEPCIS DPP-Ready: The Universal DPP Platform - harmonizing GS1, UNTP, and CIRPASS2 standards.\n\nThis vocabulary provides shared patterns reusable across domain-specific regulations\n(Battery, EUDR, Textile, Electronics, etc.) and supports the ESPR framework including:\n- Economic operator identification (EOID per ESPR Article 77)\n- Facility information (manufacturing location data)\n- Performance and durability information\n- Repairability and maintenance data\n- Substances of concern (SCIP database alignment)\n- Circularity information (end-of-life, recycling)\n- Due diligence reporting (supply chain transparency)\n- Document references (reports, certificates, guides)\n- Access rights (public vs authorized data per ESPR Article 9)\n- Emissions performance (carbon footprint with UNTP alignment)\n- Traceability performance (supply chain verification metrics)\n\nGS1 Web Vocabulary patterns to use:\n- For certifications: gs1:certification with gs1:CertificationDetails\n- For warranty: gs1:manufacturersWarranty with gs1:WarrantyPromise (product-scoped; gs1:warranty is Offer-scoped)\n- For regulatory compliance: gs1:regulatoryInformation with gs1:RegulatoryInformation\n- For documents: gs1:referencedFile with gs1:ReferencedFileDetails\n- For recycling text: gs1:consumerRecyclingInstructions\n\nUNTP Alignment:\nProperty naming, patterns, and value conventions are aligned with UN Transparency Protocol (UNTP)\nto enable native interoperability. Cross-vocabulary mappings are declared via graded SKOS relations\n(skos:exactMatch for 1:1, skos:closeMatch for approximate, skos:broadMatch where this term is narrower).\nAll ratio/fraction properties use 0-1 decimal scale (e.g., 0.45 = 45%).\n\nEPCIS 2.0 Extension Declaration:\nGS1-Extensions: oec=https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/\n\nExtension Governance:\nThis vocabulary extends GS1 Web Vocabulary only where no equivalent term exists.\nEach extension term includes:\n- dcterms:source linking to the regulatory requirement\n- skos:note explaining why the extension is needed\n- rdfs:seeAlso linking to related GS1/schema.org/UNTP terms where applicable\n- a graded SKOS mapping relation (skos:exactMatch / skos:closeMatch / skos:broadMatch) where a cross-vocabulary match exists\n\nDomain-specific vocabularies import this core and add regulation-specific extensions."@en;
    dcterms:creator "OpenEPCIS";
    dcterms:license <https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0>;
    dcterms:created "2024-01-15"^^xsd:date;
    dcterms:modified "2026-06-19"^^xsd:date;
    owl:versionInfo "0.9.9";
    owl:versionIRI <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/0.9.9>;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "oec";
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/";
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>, <https://ref.gs1.org/voc/>, gs1:CertificationDetails, gs1:WarrantyPromise, <https://ref.gs1.org/standards/epcis/>, <https://ref.gs1.org/standards/>, <https://gs1.eu/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/GDSN-Implementation-Guideline-for-exchanging-Carbon-Footprint-Data-3.pdf>, <https://untp.unece.org/docs/specification/>;
    rdfs:comment "Aligned with UN Transparency Protocol patterns"@en;
    dcterms:source <https://untp.unece.org/docs/specification/>.
oec:OperatorInformation a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:Organization, schema:Organization, <http://www.w3.org/ns/legal#LegalEntity>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Actor>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LegalPerson>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ManufacturerRecord>, <https://dpp-keystone.org/spec/v3/terms#EconomicOperatorRole>;
    rdfs:subClassOf gs1:Organization;
    rdfs:label "Operator Information"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Economic operator information as required by various EU regulations.\nCaptures manufacturer, importer, distributor, and other operator roles.\nUse gs1:globalLocationNumber for operator identification (inherited from gs1:Organization).\nUse GS1 Digital Link format: https://id.gs1.org/417/{GLN}"@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32019R1020>;
    skos:note "Extension of gs1:Organization to capture ESPR-specific operator role requirements.\nUse gs1:globalLocationNumber for operator GLN, gs1:organizationName for name.\nGS1 Web Vocabulary provides gs1:Organization but lacks the specific operator role enumeration\nrequired by EU Market Surveillance Regulation 2019/1020 and ESPR Article 77.\n\nRelated to (but NOT owl:equivalentClass with) legal:LegalEntity in the EU SEMICeu Core\nBusiness Vocabulary. The two extensions overlap but neither contains the other:\nlegal:LegalEntity is broader on the non-operator side (charities, non-profits, government\nbodies that are legal entities but not ESPR operators) and stricter on the registration\nside (some jurisdictions treat sole-proprietor operators as natural persons, not legal\nentities). Use legal:LegalEntity for EU-portal interoperability when the operator is\nknown to be a legally-registered business; the rdfs:seeAlso anchor is intentional and\nthe strongest formal claim that holds in general."@en;
    skos:broadMatch gs1:Organization, schema:Organization, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Actor>, <https://vocabulary.uncefact.org/untp/Party>.
oec:DueDiligenceReport a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Evidence>, <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Requirement>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ComplianceDeclaration>;
    rdfs:subClassOf <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Evidence>;
    rdfs:label "Due Diligence Report"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Supply chain due diligence information supporting transparency requirements.\nReusable across Battery Regulation Art. 39, EUDR, and other due diligence frameworks."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32023R1542>;
    skos:note "Required extension: GS1 Web Vocabulary does not provide a class for supply chain\ndue diligence reporting. This is mandated by EU Battery Regulation Art. 39 and EUDR.\n\nAnchored as rdfs:subClassOf cccev:Evidence (EU SEMICeu Core Criterion and Evidence\nVocabulary, http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Evidence), every due-diligence report is evidence\nsupporting a regulatory cccev:Requirement, but cccev:Evidence is much broader (test\nreports, certificates, attestations, audit logs) so the relationship is subClassOf, not\nowl:equivalentClass. CCCEV is the EU upstream of the UNTP conformity model."@en;
    skos:broadMatch <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Evidence>, schema:Report.
oec:CircularityPerformance a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:consumerRecyclingInstructions, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#CircularEconomyIndicator>;
    rdfs:label "Circularity Performance"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Information supporting circular economy requirements including\nend-of-life handling, recycling, waste prevention, and circularity metrics.\nAligned with UNTP CircularityPerformance pattern."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Required extension: GS1 provides gs1:consumerRecyclingInstructions for text-based\nrecycling guidance but lacks structured circularity data (recyclability rates, end-of-life URLs,\nwaste prevention info) required by ESPR. Use gs1:consumerRecyclingInstructions for simple text.\nAligned with UNTP CircularityPerformance for interoperability."@en.
oec:HazardousSubstance a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:hasAllergen, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Substance>;
    rdfs:label "Hazardous Substance"@en;
    rdfs:comment "A hazardous substance declaration per EU CLP Regulation 1272/2008.\nReusable across product categories."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32008R1272>;
    skos:note "Required extension: GS1 Web Vocabulary provides allergen tracking (gs1:hasAllergen)\nfor food products but lacks hazardous substance classes for industrial products per EU CLP\nRegulation 1272/2008. This class supports REACH, SCIP, and ESPR requirements."@en;
    skos:broadMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Substance>, <urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.MaterialComposition:1.2.0#HazardousSubstanceEntity>, schema:ChemicalSubstance, schema:Substance, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceOfConcern>.
oec:DocumentReference a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:ReferencedFileDetails, <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#DigitalInstruction>;
    rdfs:label "Document Reference"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Reference to an external document such as reports, certificates,\nmanuals, or guides. Supports multiple languages and formats.\nSee also gs1:ReferencedFileDetails for GS1 Web Vocabulary equivalent."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    skos:note "PREFER gs1:ReferencedFileDetails where possible. This class provides equivalent\nfunctionality with additional ESPR-specific document types. Use gs1:referencedFile\nproperty with gs1:ReferencedFileDetails for standard documents (manuals, certificates).\nUse oec:DocumentReference only when ESPR-specific document types are required."@en;
    skos:broadMatch <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document>;
    skos:closeMatch gs1:ReferencedFileDetails.
oec:RecycledContent a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://gs1.eu/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/GDSN-Implementation-Guideline-for-exchanging-Carbon-Footprint-Data-3.pdf>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#RecycledMaterialsUseResult>, <urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.Circularity:1.2.0#RecycledContentEntity>, gs1:PackagingDetails;
    rdfs:label "Recycled Content"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Declaration of recycled material content with pre-consumer\nand post-consumer splits."@en;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Required extension: GS1 Web Vocabulary does not provide structured recycled content\nproperties. ESPR and Battery Regulation require pre-consumer/post-consumer breakdown which is\nnot available in GS1 vocabulary. Aligned with GDSN sustainability attributes."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#RecycledContentDeclaration>.
oec:MaterialComposition a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:TextileMaterialDetails, gs1:PackagingMaterialDetails, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaterialOfComposition>;
    rdfs:label "Material Composition"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Material composition information including source country,\npercentage, and critical raw material classification."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Required extension: GS1 provides gs1:TextileMaterialDetails and\ngs1:PackagingMaterialDetails for specific domains but lacks a generic material composition\nclass with CAS/EC number support and critical raw material flags required by ESPR."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch gs1:TextileMaterialDetails, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#FibreCompositionComponent>.
oec:FacilityInformation a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:Place, schema:Place, <https://vocabulary.uncefact.org/untp/Facility>, <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#Location>, <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#Address>, <http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#Geometry>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Facility>, <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/InformationConcept>;
    rdfs:subClassOf gs1:Place;
    rdfs:label "Facility Information"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Manufacturing or processing facility information per ESPR.\nCaptures facility identification, location, and certification data.\nUse gs1:globalLocationNumber for facility identification, schema:name for facility name, gs1:address for location (all inherited from gs1:Place).\nUse GS1 Digital Link format: https://id.gs1.org/414/{GLN}"@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Extension of gs1:Place to capture ESPR-specific facility requirements.\nUse gs1:globalLocationNumber for facility GLN identification, schema:name for facility name, gs1:address for location.\nGS1 provides gs1:Place but lacks facility certification and type properties required by ESPR.\nAligned with UNTP Facility for Digital Facility Record (DFR) interoperability.\nAnchored to locn:Location (EU SEMICeu Core Location Vocabulary, http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#)\nfor EU-portal interoperability: locn:Address and locn:Geometry are the canonical\nsub-structures for the address and geographic-coordinate parts."@en;
    skos:broadMatch gs1:Place, schema:Place.
oec:SubstanceOfConcern a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#SubstanceOfConcern>, <https://echa.europa.eu/scip-database>;
    rdfs:subClassOf oec:HazardousSubstance;
    rdfs:label "Substance of Concern"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances of concern declaration aligned with SCIP database\nand ESPR requirements. Extends HazardousSubstance for detailed tracking."@en;
    dcterms:source <https://echa.europa.eu/scip>;
    skos:note "Required extension: SCIP database integration requires specific fields (SCIP ID,\nEC Number, safe use instructions) not available in GS1 Web Vocabulary. Supports REACH Article 33\nand Waste Framework Directive requirements."@en;
    skos:broadMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Substance>, <urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.MaterialComposition:1.2.0#HazardousSubstanceEntity>, schema:ChemicalSubstance, schema:Substance.
oec:PerformanceInfo a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:manufacturersWarranty, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability>, <https://vocabulary.uncefact.org/untp/PerformanceMetric>;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/assessment/Assessment>;
    rdfs:label "Performance Information"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Product performance and durability assessment per ESPR Article 7. An oea:Assessment:\nexpected lifespan, technical lifetime, usage cycles and performance class are indicators\n(oea:hasIndicator with oea:ExpectedLifetime, oea:TechnicalLifetime, oea:NumberOfUseCycles,\noea:PerformanceClass), measured performance values are results (oea:hasResult), and the test\nconditions are oea:hasCondition. Sector modules hang their own performance properties here."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Required extension: GS1 provides gs1:manufacturersWarranty for warranty information but lacks\nstructured performance and durability data required by ESPR Article 7. Since 0.9.9 the values travel\nthrough the oea: assessment model rather than flat properties (oec:usageCycles, oec:hasExpectedLifespan,\noec:hasTechnicalLifetime, oec:performanceClass and oec:testedConditions were removed). Use in\nconjunction with gs1:manufacturersWarranty where applicable."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#PerformanceAfterNCycles>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/battery-performance#BatteryDurability>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#PerformanceRetentionRate>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/battery-performance#BatteryPerformance>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#SurfacePerformanceParameter>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#AssemblyPerformanceParameter>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-indicator#PerformanceLevelOverTime>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-durability#MechanicalPerformanceParameter>.
oec:RepairabilityInfo a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:referencedFile, gs1:manufacturersWarranty, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Durability>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Reliability>;
    rdfs:label "Repairability Information"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Repair and maintenance information per ESPR Article 7: spare part availability,\nsoftware update support, repair instructions and services. A repairability score or class is an\nindicator (oea:hasIndicator with oea:RepairabilityScore or oea:RepairabilityClass)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Required extension: ESPR Article 7 mandates repairability scores (French Indice de\nRéparabilité style), spare parts availability periods, and DIY repair information not available\nin GS1 Web Vocabulary. Use gs1:referencedFile for repair manuals."@en.
oec:AccessRights a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:label "Access Rights"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Access control for DPP data per ESPR Article 9.\nDefines which data is publicly accessible vs. restricted to authorized parties."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Required extension: ESPR Article 9 defines three access levels (Public, Authorized,\nRestricted) for DPP data. GS1 Web Vocabulary does not provide access control semantics.\nThis supports the ESPR requirement for tiered data access."@en.
oec:EmissionsPerformance a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://gs1.eu/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/GDSN-Implementation-Guideline-for-exchanging-Carbon-Footprint-Data-3.pdf>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAResult>;
    rdfs:label "Emissions Performance"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Container for greenhouse gas emissions data including carbon footprint,\nlifecycle phases, and verification status. Aligned with UNTP EmissionsPerformance."@en;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Required extension: Structured emissions performance data for ESPR requirements.\nAligned with UNTP EmissionsPerformance for interoperability. Extends the GDSN CFP pattern\nwith operational scope and verification metrics."@en;
    skos:narrowMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#CarbonFootprint>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#LCIAResult>.
oec:TraceabilityPerformance a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://vocabulary.uncefact.org/untp/PerformanceMetric>;
    rdfs:label "Traceability Performance"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Supply chain verification and traceability metrics indicating the proportion\nof materials that are verifiably traced through the supply chain."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Required extension: ESPR and due diligence regulations require traceability metrics.\nAligned with UNTP TraceabilityPerformance for supply chain transparency reporting."@en;
    skos:broadMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#QuantitativeProperty>.
oec:OperatorRole a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EconomicOperatorRole>, schema:OrganizationRole;
    rdfs:subClassOf oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Operator Role"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Role of an economic operator in the supply chain. The six ESPR / EN 18239:2026 4.2(1) economic-operator sub-roles (manufacturer, authorised representative, importer, distributor, dealer, fulfilment service provider) plus the EUDR (EU) 2023/1115 Art. 2 supply-chain positions (producer, operator, trader, downstream operator) and processor; every member is also an oec:ActorRole. One role vocabulary for every regulation module - no module mints its own."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    owl:oneOf _:b8.
oec:ActorRole a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EconomicOperatorRole>, schema:OrganizationRole;
    rdfs:label "Actor Role"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Role an organisation or individual fulfils along the DPP life cycle, as\nenumerated by EN 18239:2026 4.2: economic operators and their sub-roles (oec:OperatorRole),\nthe other value-chain actors (consumer, professional repairer, independent operator,\nrecycler, market surveillance authority), customs authorities and DPP service providers -\nplus the notified actor of 3.6. Access rights to controlled DPP data are granted to these\nroles (EN 18239 5.2.7, 5.2.8, 5.2.23)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)";
    skos:note "Roles are what a credential attests and what a policy names; they are not tenant membership. An economic operator reading its own passport data is the data controller and is never gated by a role list - role gating governs actors OTHER than the owning operator."@en;
    owl:oneOf _:b9.
_:b8 rdf:first oec:Manufacturer;
    rdf:rest _:b10.
oec:Manufacturer a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Manufacturer"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity that produces the product, including own-brand labellers per EU Market Surveillance Regulation 2019/1020."@en.
_:b10 rdf:first oec:AuthorisedRepresentative;
    rdf:rest _:b11.
oec:AuthorisedRepresentative a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#AuthorisedRepresentativeRoleAssignment>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#hasAuthorisedRepresentative>;
    rdfs:label "Authorised Representative"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity authorised by manufacturer to act on their behalf for specific tasks (per ESPR Article 16)."@en.
_:b11 rdf:first oec:Importer;
    rdf:rest _:b12.
oec:Importer a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Importer"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity established in the EU that places a product from a third country on the Union market."@en.
_:b12 rdf:first oec:Distributor;
    rdf:rest _:b13.
oec:Distributor a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Distributor"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity in the supply chain that makes a product available on the market, other than manufacturer or importer."@en.
_:b13 rdf:first oec:Dealer;
    rdf:rest _:b14.
oec:Dealer a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Dealer"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Distributor or any other natural or legal person that offers products for sale, hire or hire purchase, or displays them to end users in the course of a commercial activity, including distance selling and putting into service (ESPR Art. 2; EN 18239:2026 4.2(1)(e))."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
_:b14 rdf:first oec:FulfilmentServiceProvider;
    rdf:rest _:b15.
oec:FulfilmentServiceProvider a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Fulfilment Service Provider"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity providing fulfilment services including warehousing and order processing (per ESPR Article 17)."@en.
_:b15 rdf:first oec:Processor;
    rdf:rest _:b16.
oec:Processor a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Processor"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity that processes raw materials or components into finished or intermediate products."@en.
_:b16 rdf:first oec:Trader;
    rdf:rest _:b17.
oec:Trader a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Trader"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity that buys and sells products without significant modification or processing; under EUDR (EU) 2023/1115 Art. 2(17) the person who makes products available on the market after the operator."@en;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1115>.
_:b17 rdf:first oec:Producer;
    rdf:rest _:b18.
oec:Producer a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Producer"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity that produces or harvests the commodity at the start of the chain (EUDR (EU) 2023/1115 supply-chain position; moved here from the former eudr:ActorRole)."@en;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1115>.
_:b18 rdf:first oec:Operator;
    rdf:rest _:b19.
oec:Operator a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Operator"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity that places products on the EU market or exports them from it (EUDR (EU) 2023/1115 Art. 2(15)); the EUDR name for the economic operator placing on the market, kept for EUDR records."@en;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1115>.
_:b19 rdf:first oec:DownstreamOperator;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
oec:DownstreamOperator a oec:OperatorRole, oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Downstream Operator"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Entity that receives products already placed on the EU market and makes them available further downstream, subject to simplified due-diligence obligations (introduced by the December 2025 EUDR amendment)."@en;
    dcterms:source <https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/press/press-releases/2025/12/18/deforestation-council-signs-off-targeted-revision-to-simplify-and-postpone-the-regulation/>;
    skos:note "Downstream operators have reduced due-diligence obligations compared to operators."@en.
_:b9 rdf:first oec:Manufacturer;
    rdf:rest _:b20.
_:b20 rdf:first oec:AuthorisedRepresentative;
    rdf:rest _:b21.
_:b21 rdf:first oec:Importer;
    rdf:rest _:b22.
_:b22 rdf:first oec:Distributor;
    rdf:rest _:b23.
_:b23 rdf:first oec:Dealer;
    rdf:rest _:b24.
_:b24 rdf:first oec:FulfilmentServiceProvider;
    rdf:rest _:b25.
_:b25 rdf:first oec:Processor;
    rdf:rest _:b26.
_:b26 rdf:first oec:Trader;
    rdf:rest _:b27.
_:b27 rdf:first oec:Producer;
    rdf:rest _:b28.
_:b28 rdf:first oec:Operator;
    rdf:rest _:b29.
_:b29 rdf:first oec:DownstreamOperator;
    rdf:rest _:b30.
_:b30 rdf:first oec:Consumer;
    rdf:rest _:b31.
oec:Consumer a oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Consumer"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Individual member of the general public purchasing or using goods, property or services for private purposes (EN ISO 14025:2010, 3.16; EN 18239:2026 4.2(2)(a)). Reads public DPP data without authentication (EN 18239 5.2.2)."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
_:b31 rdf:first oec:ProfessionalRepairer;
    rdf:rest _:b32.
oec:ProfessionalRepairer a oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Professional Repairer"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Natural or legal person providing professional repair or maintenance services for a product, whether within the manufacturer's distribution system or independently (EN 18239:2026 4.2(2)(b))."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
_:b32 rdf:first oec:IndependentOperator;
    rdf:rest _:b33.
oec:IndependentOperator a oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Independent Operator"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Natural or legal person independent of the manufacturer and directly or indirectly involved in refurbishment, repair, maintenance or repurposing of a product - including waste management operators, refurbishers, repairers, makers or distributors of repair equipment, tools or spare parts, publishers of technical information, inspection and testing services, and trainers (EN 18239:2026 4.2(2)(c))."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
_:b33 rdf:first oec:Recycler;
    rdf:rest _:b34.
oec:Recycler a oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Recycler"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Natural or legal person responsible for the collection, processing and recovery of reusable materials and applying a decontamination process (EN 18239:2026 4.2(2)(d))."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
_:b34 rdf:first oec:MarketSurveillanceAuthority;
    rdf:rest _:b35.
oec:MarketSurveillanceAuthority a oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Market Surveillance Authority"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Authority designated by a Member State as responsible for carrying out market surveillance in its territory (Regulation (EU) 2019/1020; EN 18239:2026 4.2(2)(e))."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
_:b35 rdf:first oec:CustomsAuthority;
    rdf:rest _:b36.
oec:CustomsAuthority a oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:label "Customs Authority"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Government service responsible for administering customs law, collecting duties and taxes, and applying other laws on the import, export, movement or storage of goods (EN 18239:2026 4.2(3))."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
_:b36 rdf:first oec:DppServiceProvider;
    rdf:rest _:b37.
oec:DppServiceProvider a oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:seeAlso oec:hasBackupCopyHost;
    rdfs:label "DPP Service Provider"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Independent third party authorised by the economic operator that processes the DPP data for a product to make it available to actors with a right to access it - hosting the main instance or the back-up copy (EN 18221:2026, 3.2-3.3; EN 18239:2026 4.2(4)(a))."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 4.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
_:b37 rdf:first oec:NotifiedActor;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
oec:NotifiedActor a oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#hasNotifiedBody>;
    rdfs:label "Notified Actor"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Organisation or individual entitled by an authorised accrediting body or authority to fulfil a role in the DPP life cycle (EN 18239:2026 3.6) - notified bodies and conformity assessment bodies in particular. The EO may assign rights and roles to notified actors by their globally unique operator identifier (EN 18239 5.2.6)."@en;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 3.6 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)".
oec:hasBackupCopyHost a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso oec:hasPassportIssuer, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#hasBackUpCopyHost>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppBackupUrl>;
    rdfs:label "Backup Copy Host"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Digital product passport service provider that holds the backup copy of this passport, ensuring availability if the primary host fails or the responsible economic operator ceases to exist."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "ESPR Art. 10(4) requires a backup copy of the passport to be available through a DPP service provider. Neither GS1, SEMICeu nor schema.org carries a backup-custodian role; schema:issuedBy names the issuer, not the fallback host."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#hasBackUpCopyHost>;
    rdfs:range oec:OperatorInformation.
oec:AccessLevel a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:label "Access Level"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Access levels for DPP data per ESPR Article 9."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    owl:oneOf _:b38.
_:b38 rdf:first oec:Public;
    rdf:rest _:b39.
oec:Public a oec:AccessLevel;
    rdfs:label "Public"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Data accessible to all users (consumers, market surveillance, customs). Per ESPR Article 9(1)."@en.
_:b39 rdf:first oec:AuthorizedOnly;
    rdf:rest _:b40.
oec:AuthorizedOnly a oec:AccessLevel;
    rdfs:label "Authorized Only"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Data accessible only to market surveillance authorities and customs. Per ESPR Article 9(2)."@en.
_:b40 rdf:first oec:Restricted;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
oec:Restricted a oec:AccessLevel;
    rdfs:label "Restricted"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Data accessible only to specific authorized economic operators. Per ESPR Article 9(3)."@en.
oec:defaultAccessLevel a owl:AnnotationProperty;
    rdfs:label "default access level"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Default ESPR Article 9 access tier for values of the annotated property in\nDPP / master-data documents (Public, AuthorizedOnly, Restricted). Deployments may tighten a\nfield's tier at runtime but never loosen it below this default. Properties without this\nannotation default to AuthorizedOnly (fail-closed toward the public)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "Field-level counterpart of oec:hasAccessLevel: while oec:hasAccessLevel classifies a\ndocument instance via its AccessRights object, oec:defaultAccessLevel classifies the property\ndefinition itself. Generators carry it into JSON Schemas as x-access-level and into the\nvocabulary browser JSON as accessLevel."@en;
    rdfs:range oec:AccessLevel.
oec:accessLevelMandatedBy a owl:AnnotationProperty;
    rdfs:label "access level mandated by"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Legal act that fixes the access tier of the annotated property. Presence of\nthis annotation makes the oec:defaultAccessLevel non-overridable at runtime (locked in both\ndirections)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Resource.
oec:accessGrantedToRole a owl:AnnotationProperty;
    rdfs:label "access granted to role"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Actor roles (EN 18239:2026 4.2) that the legal act named in\noec:accessLevelMandatedBy admits to the annotated property. Multi-valued. Only meaningful\ntogether with oec:accessLevelMandatedBy: it FIXES the audience of the term - EN 18239 5.2.7\nhas the product-group legal act define the roles that grant access to regulated data, so an\neconomic operator may neither widen nor narrow this set at runtime. Terms without it fall\nback to the module's tier-level role defaults (oec:authorizedOnlyGrantedToRole /\noec:restrictedGrantedToRole), and for non-mandated terms the economic operator may grant\nadditional roles. Role gating never applies to the economic operator reading its own data:\nit governs OTHER actors' access (EN 18239 5.2.8 - a trustworthy role credential admits an\nactor without the EO's individual approval)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 5.2 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)";
    rdfs:range oec:ActorRole.
oec:authorizedOnlyGrantedToRole a owl:AnnotationProperty;
    rdfs:label "AuthorizedOnly tier granted to role"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Module-level default, stated on the module's owl:Ontology node in its\n*-access-levels.ttl sidecar: the actor roles the module's governing legal act admits to\nAuthorizedOnly-tier data as a whole. Applies to every AuthorizedOnly term of the module that\ncarries no oec:accessGrantedToRole of its own. A module without this statement inherits the\ndpp-core defaults (ESPR Art. 9)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 5.2.7 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)";
    rdfs:range oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:domain owl:Ontology.
oec:restrictedGrantedToRole a owl:AnnotationProperty;
    rdfs:label "Restricted tier granted to role"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Module-level default, stated on the module's owl:Ontology node in its\n*-access-levels.ttl sidecar: the actor roles the module's governing legal act admits to\nRestricted-tier data as a whole. Applies to every Restricted term of the module that carries\nno oec:accessGrantedToRole of its own. A module without this statement inherits the dpp-core\ndefaults (ESPR Art. 9(3): authorities and notified actors)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source "EN 18239:2026, 5.2.7 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)";
    rdfs:range oec:ActorRole;
    rdfs:domain owl:Ontology.
oec:accessLevelRationale a owl:AnnotationProperty;
    rdfs:label "access level rationale"@en;
    rdfs:comment "One-sentence justification for the annotated property's\noec:defaultAccessLevel — why this tier, in terms a reviewer or auditor can check\nagainst the underlying regulation. REQUIRED wherever oec:defaultAccessLevel is\nset (enforced by check-access-levels). Rendered on ref.openepcis.org term pages\nand in the DDM field-access matrix."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    rdfs:range xsd:string.
oec:accessLevelSource a owl:AnnotationProperty;
    rdfs:label "access level source"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Legal act or article that GROUNDS the tier decision (citation).\nUnlike oec:accessLevelMandatedBy it does NOT lock the tier — it documents where\nthe default came from. Use an ELI/CELEX IRI, as specific as available."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    rdfs:range rdfs:Resource.
oec:accessLevelInherited a owl:AnnotationProperty;
    rdfs:label "access level inherited"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Marks a structural value-carrier sub-property (value, unit,\ndocument URL, ...) that has NO tier of its own: at runtime its visibility is\ngoverned entirely by the embedding parent property's tier. Declaring it keeps\nthe vocabulary 100% explicitly classified (the completeness guard accepts\naccessLevelInherited in lieu of defaultAccessLevel) without inventing a fake\ntier, and keeps such terms out of the enforcement alias map."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean.
oec:PassportStatus a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppStatus>;
    rdfs:label "Passport Status"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Lifecycle status of a Digital Product Passport (EN 18223 dppStatus). Values are the lowercase string tokens given by skos:notation."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source "EN 18223:2026, 4.1.2.1 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)";
    skos:note "Base values active/inactive/archived/invalid per EN 18223 Table 1; draft/withdrawn/suspended are EPCIS4DPP profile extensions permitted by 'further values by relevant legal acts'."@en;
    skos:broadMatch schema:StatusEnumeration;
    owl:oneOf _:b41.
_:b41 rdf:first oec:Active;
    rdf:rest _:b42.
oec:Active a oec:PassportStatus;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/Disp-active>;
    rdfs:label "Active"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Passport is published and represents the current state of the product."@en;
    skos:notation "active".
_:b42 rdf:first oec:Inactive;
    rdf:rest _:b43.
oec:Inactive a oec:PassportStatus;
    rdfs:label "Inactive"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Passport is not currently in force (EN 18223 base value)."@en;
    skos:notation "inactive".
_:b43 rdf:first oec:Archived;
    rdf:rest _:b44.
oec:Archived a oec:PassportStatus;
    rdfs:label "Archived"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Passport is archived after product end-of-life. Data persisted per EN 18221."@en;
    skos:notation "archived".
_:b44 rdf:first oec:Invalid;
    rdf:rest _:b45.
oec:Invalid a oec:PassportStatus;
    rdfs:label "Invalid"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Passport is no longer valid (EN 18223 base value, e.g. revoked)."@en;
    skos:notation "invalid".
_:b45 rdf:first oec:Draft;
    rdf:rest _:b46.
oec:Draft a oec:PassportStatus;
    rdfs:label "Draft"@en;
    rdfs:comment "EPCIS4DPP extension: passport is being prepared and not yet publicly available."@en;
    skos:notation "draft".
_:b46 rdf:first oec:Withdrawn;
    rdf:rest _:b47.
oec:Withdrawn a oec:PassportStatus;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/Disp-recalled>;
    rdfs:label "Withdrawn"@en;
    rdfs:comment "EPCIS4DPP extension: passport withdrawn (e.g. product recall); a specific kind of invalid."@en;
    skos:notation "withdrawn".
_:b47 rdf:first oec:Suspended;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
oec:Suspended a oec:PassportStatus;
    rdfs:label "Suspended"@en;
    rdfs:comment "EPCIS4DPP extension: temporarily not in force (e.g. pending investigation); a specific kind of inactive."@en;
    skos:notation "suspended".
oec:BizStep-notifying a <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep-inspecting>;
    rdfs:label "Notifying"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Submitting a regulatory notification, declaration or statement about the product to a competent authority — an EUDR due-diligence or exemption declaration, a Battery Regulation notification, an ESPR conformity notification."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1115>;
    skos:note "CBV 2.0 publishes no business step for reporting to an authority; its 41 values cover physical and commercial handling only, and cbv:BizStep-other would drop the distinction. Carried by at least two regulation modules (EUDR declarations, Battery Regulation notifications), so it belongs in the DPP core rather than one module."@en;
    skos:notation "notifying".
oec:BizStep-recovery a <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep-destroying>;
    rdfs:label "Recovery"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Recovering material or energy from a product at end of life, e.g. reprocessing collected packaging into secondary raw material."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2025/40>;
    skos:note "CBV 2.0 has no recovery or recycling business step: cbv:BizStep-destroying and cbv:BizStep-disassembling describe different operations and would misstate the process. Cross-regulation (PPWR material recovery, Battery Regulation recycling, WEEE treatment), so DPP core rather than a module."@en;
    skos:notation "recovery".
oec:BizStep-maintaining a <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep-inspecting>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#MaintenanceEvent>;
    rdfs:label "Maintaining"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Actions (one or more) taken to keep a product in a condition where it can fulfil its intended purpose (ESPR Art. 2(19))."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "CBV 2.0 (verified against the live vocabulary 2026-08-06) has no maintenance business step: cbv:BizStep-inspecting is examination without intervention, cbv:BizStep-repairing presupposes a defect, while ESPR maintenance is preventive. ESPR is horizontal, so DPP core rather than a module. CIRPASS-2's EUDPP EVENT module wraps the same Art. 2(19) definition in an event class (cirpass2:MaintenanceEvent); modelled here as CBV vocabulary because the definition describes an activity, not an event."@en;
    skos:notation "maintaining".
oec:BizStep-refurbishing a <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep-repairing>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#RefurbishmentEvent>;
    rdfs:label "Refurbishing"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Actions carried out to prepare, clean, test, service and, where necessary, repair a product or a discarded product in order to restore its performance or functionality within the intended use and range of performance originally conceived at the design stage (ESPR Art. 2(18))."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "CBV 2.0 (verified 2026-08-06) has no refurbishing business step: cbv:BizStep-repairing covers returning a defective product to service, while refurbishment restores performance of a possibly non-defective or discarded product within its original design envelope. Cross-regulation (ESPR horizontal, Battery Regulation Art. 2(26)), so DPP core. CIRPASS-2 wraps the same Art. 2(18) definition in cirpass2:RefurbishmentEvent."@en;
    skos:notation "refurbishing".
oec:BizStep-remanufacturing a <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep-commissioning>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#RemanufacturingEvent>;
    rdfs:label "Remanufacturing"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Actions through which a new product is produced from objects that are waste, products or components and through which at least one change is made that substantially affects the safety, performance, purpose or type of the product (ESPR Art. 2(16))."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "CBV 2.0 (verified 2026-08-06) has no remanufacturing business step. Belongs on an EPCIS TransformationEvent, not an ObjectEvent: per the ESPR definition remanufacturing produces a NEW product from waste/components, so the output carries a new identity (input/output EPC lists), which an event-class taxonomy like cirpass2:RemanufacturingEvent (subclass of ProductEvent) cannot express. ESPR horizontal, so DPP core."@en;
    skos:notation "remanufacturing".
oec:BizStep-upgrading a <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/BizStep-repairing>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#UpgradingEvent>;
    rdfs:label "Upgrading"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Actions carried out to enhance the functionality, performance, capacity, safety or aesthetics of a product (ESPR Art. 2(17))."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "CBV 2.0 (verified 2026-08-06) has no upgrading business step: cbv:BizStep-repairing restores intended function, while upgrading enhances beyond the original state. ESPR horizontal, so DPP core. CIRPASS-2 wraps the same Art. 2(17) definition in cirpass2:UpgradingEvent."@en;
    skos:notation "upgrading".
oec:Disp-subject_to_regulation a <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/Disp>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/Disp-conformant>;
    rdfs:label "Subject to regulation"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The item is within the scope of a product regulation and carries the corresponding obligations (e.g. an EUDR-relevant commodity). Set as a persistentDisposition so it travels with the item across events."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2023/1115>;
    skos:note "CBV 2.0's 33 dispositions describe physical/commercial state (active, in_transit, recalled, …); none expresses regulatory scope. Carried by the EUDR declaration events and applicable to any regulation module, so DPP core rather than a module."@en;
    skos:notation "subject_to_regulation".
oec:Disp-available_on_market a <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/Disp>;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://ref.gs1.org/cbv/Disp-active>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#MakingAvailableOnMarketEvent>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#PlacingOnMarketEvent>;
    rdfs:label "Available on the market"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The product is supplied for distribution, consumption or use on the Union market in the course of a commercial activity (ESPR Art. 2(39)). Set as a persistentDisposition so the market status travels with the item across events; the event that first sets it records the placing on the market (Art. 2(40))."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "CBV 2.0 (verified 2026-08-06) has no market-status disposition. Making available / placing on the market are legal acts, not observable operations: modelled as a persistent state rather than a business step, because 'is on the Union market' persists across subsequent events while the act itself coincides with an ordinary shipping or selling event. CIRPASS-2 wraps the same definitions in cirpass2:MakingAvailableOnMarketEvent / cirpass2:PlacingOnMarketEvent."@en;
    skos:notation "available_on_market".
oec:DPPGranularity a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:label "DPP Granularity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Reporting granularity of a Digital Product Passport: which level of the product hierarchy a given attribute set describes."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://thebatterypass.eu/battery-pass-ready/publications/>;
    skos:note "Introduced by BatteryPass-Ready Data Attribute Longlist v1.3 (March 2026) to align EU Battery Passport reporting with CEN/CENELEC JTC-24 drafts. Some attributes (e.g. recycled-content shares, carbon-footprint label) are reported at batch level, others at model or item level."@en;
    owl:oneOf _:b48.
_:b48 rdf:first oec:ModelLevel;
    rdf:rest _:b49.
oec:ModelLevel a oec:DPPGranularity;
    rdfs:label "Battery model"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Attribute reported once per battery model (e.g. nominal voltage, expected cycle life). Model master data has a single source of truth: the same model built at different manufacturing sites is NOT a distinct granularity level. Site is a source/location dimension carried by EPCIS events (readPoint / bizLocation); facts that vary per production run are reported at BatchLevel."@en.
_:b49 rdf:first oec:BatchLevel;
    rdf:rest _:b50.
oec:BatchLevel a oec:DPPGranularity;
    rdfs:label "Battery model per calendar year and per manufacturing site (batch)"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Attribute reported per batch: model, calendar year, manufacturing site (e.g. carbon footprint, recycled-content shares)."@en.
_:b50 rdf:first oec:ItemLevel;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
oec:ItemLevel a oec:DPPGranularity;
    rdfs:label "Individual battery item"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Attribute reported per individual serial-numbered battery (e.g. serial number, state of health, cycle count)."@en.
oec:hasReportingGranularity a owl:ObjectProperty;
    rdfs:label "Reporting Granularity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "BatteryPass per-attribute reporting granularity (model / model-per-site / batch / item). Distinct from the passport-level EN 18223 'granularity' (oec:granularityLevel)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://thebatterypass.eu/battery-pass-ready/publications/>;
    skos:note "BatteryPass-Ready v1.3 longlist attribute #3. Renamed from oec:granularity to free the 'granularity' key for the EN 18223 passport-level attribute (oec:granularityLevel)."@en;
    skos:closeMatch <https://dpp-keystone.org/spec/v3/terms#granularity>, <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/core/vocabs/core-vocabulary#granularity>;
    rdfs:range oec:DPPGranularity;
    rdfs:domain gs1:Product.
oec:lastUpdated a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:label "Last Updated"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Date and time of the latest update to the DPP instance (EN 18223 lastUpdated), UTC, ISO 8601."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source "EN 18223:2026, 4.1.2.1 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)";
    skos:note "Consolidates the former oec:lastUpdate (BatteryPass-Ready v1.3 #4), oec:passportLastModified, oec:lastDataUpdate and eubat:lastDataUpdate into the EN 18223 'lastUpdated' attribute."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://ref.openepcis.org/vocab/batterypass-ready/1.3#Date-timeOfLatestUpdateOfDPP>, <https://dpp-keystone.org/spec/v3/terms#lastUpdate>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#lastUpdate>, <https://repository.product-passport.ec.europa.eu/core/vocabs/core-vocabulary#lastUpdate>;
    skos:closeMatch <urn:samm:io.BatteryPass.Performance:1.2.1#lastUpdate>;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime;
    rdfs:domain oec:DigitalProductPassport.
oec:DigitalProductPassport a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPPEvent>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#dppUrl>;
    rdfs:label "Digital Product Passport"@en;
    rdfs:comment "The DPP envelope: identification and lifecycle metadata plus the product data elements, per the EN 18223 information model."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source "EN 18223:2026, 4.1.2.1 (CEN/CENELEC JTC 24)";
    skos:note "EN 18223 DigitalProductPassport. Attributes: digitalProductPassportId (oec:passportIdentifier), uniqueProductIdentifier, granularity (oec:granularityLevel), dppSchemaVersion, dppStatus (oec:passportStatus), lastUpdated, economicOperatorId, facilityId, contentSpecificationIds, plus product data elements."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#DPP>, <https://dpp-keystone.org/spec/v3/terms#DigitalProductPassport>;
    skos:broadMatch schema:DigitalDocument.
oec:ProductCategory a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:Product, schema:Product, gs1:FoodBeverageTobaccoProduct, <https://dpp-keystone.org/spec/v3/terms#BatteryProduct>;
    rdfs:label "Product Category"@en;
    rdfs:comment "ESPR priority product categories per Annex I and delegated acts."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:broadMatch schema:CategoryCode;
    owl:oneOf _:b51.
_:b51 rdf:first oec:Batteries;
    rdf:rest _:b52.
oec:Batteries a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Batteries"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Batteries and accumulators per EU Battery Regulation 2023/1542."@en.
_:b52 rdf:first oec:Textiles;
    rdf:rest _:b53.
oec:Textiles a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Textiles"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Textile products including apparel, footwear, and home textiles."@en.
_:b53 rdf:first oec:Electronics;
    rdf:rest _:b54.
oec:Electronics a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Electronics"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Electronic and electrical equipment including ICT and consumer electronics."@en.
_:b54 rdf:first oec:Furniture;
    rdf:rest _:b55.
oec:Furniture a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Furniture"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Furniture products including domestic and office furniture."@en.
_:b55 rdf:first oec:Tyres;
    rdf:rest _:b56.
oec:Tyres a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Tyres"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Tyres for motor vehicles and their trailers."@en.
_:b56 rdf:first oec:ConstructionProducts;
    rdf:rest _:b57.
oec:ConstructionProducts a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Construction Products"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Construction products per Construction Products Regulation."@en.
_:b57 rdf:first oec:Chemicals;
    rdf:rest _:b58.
oec:Chemicals a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Chemicals"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Chemical substances and mixtures."@en.
_:b58 rdf:first oec:Detergents;
    rdf:rest _:b59.
oec:Detergents a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:RegulationTypeCode-DETERGENTS_SAFETY_REGULATION;
    rdfs:label "Detergents"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Detergents and surfactants per the EU Detergents Regulation (EU) 2026/405, an ESPR priority product category."@en;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32026R0405>.
_:b59 rdf:first oec:Packaging;
    rdf:rest _:b60.
oec:Packaging a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Packaging"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Packaging and packaging waste products."@en.
_:b60 rdf:first oec:FoodContact;
    rdf:rest _:b61.
oec:FoodContact a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Food Contact Materials"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Materials and articles intended for food contact."@en.
_:b61 rdf:first oec:IronSteel;
    rdf:rest _:b62.
oec:IronSteel a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Iron and Steel"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Iron and steel intermediate products."@en.
_:b62 rdf:first oec:Aluminium;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
oec:Aluminium a oec:ProductCategory;
    rdfs:label "Aluminium"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Aluminium intermediate products."@en.
oec:HazardClass a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:label "Hazard Class"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Hazard classification categories per EU CLP Regulation."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32008R1272>;
    owl:oneOf _:b63.
_:b63 rdf:first oec:AcuteToxicity;
    rdf:rest _:b64.
oec:AcuteToxicity a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Acute Toxicity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances causing harmful effects after single or short-term exposure via oral, dermal, or inhalation routes."@en.
_:b64 rdf:first oec:SkinCorrosionOrIrritation;
    rdf:rest _:b65.
oec:SkinCorrosionOrIrritation a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Skin Corrosion or Irritation"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances causing irreversible damage (corrosion) or reversible damage (irritation) to skin tissue."@en.
_:b65 rdf:first oec:EyeDamageOrIrritation;
    rdf:rest _:b66.
oec:EyeDamageOrIrritation a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Eye Damage or Irritation"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances causing serious eye damage or reversible eye irritation upon contact."@en.
_:b66 rdf:first oec:RespiratoryOrSkinSensitization;
    rdf:rest _:b67.
oec:RespiratoryOrSkinSensitization a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Respiratory or Skin Sensitization"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances causing hypersensitivity of airways (asthma) or allergic skin reactions after exposure."@en.
_:b67 rdf:first oec:GermCellMutagenicity;
    rdf:rest _:b68.
oec:GermCellMutagenicity a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Germ Cell Mutagenicity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances that may cause heritable genetic mutations in human germ cells."@en.
_:b68 rdf:first oec:Carcinogenicity;
    rdf:rest _:b69.
oec:Carcinogenicity a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Carcinogenicity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances known or suspected to cause cancer in humans."@en.
_:b69 rdf:first oec:ReproductiveToxicity;
    rdf:rest _:b70.
oec:ReproductiveToxicity a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Reproductive Toxicity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances adversely affecting sexual function, fertility, or development of offspring."@en.
_:b70 rdf:first oec:SpecificTargetOrganToxicity;
    rdf:rest _:b71.
oec:SpecificTargetOrganToxicity a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Specific Target Organ Toxicity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances causing non-lethal damage to specific organs after single or repeated exposure."@en.
_:b71 rdf:first oec:AspirationHazard;
    rdf:rest _:b72.
oec:AspirationHazard a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Aspiration Hazard"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Liquid or solid substances causing chemical pneumonia or pulmonary injury if aspirated into airways."@en.
_:b72 rdf:first oec:HazardousToAquaticEnvironment;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
oec:HazardousToAquaticEnvironment a oec:HazardClass;
    rdfs:label "Hazardous to Aquatic Environment"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Substances posing acute or chronic toxicity risks to aquatic organisms and ecosystems."@en.
oec:DocumentType a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso gs1:ReferencedFileTypeCode, schema:SpreadsheetDigitalDocument;
    rdfs:label "Document Type"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Types of supporting documents for DPP.\nSee also gs1:ReferencedFileTypeCode for GS1 standard document types (PRODUCT_MANUAL, SAFETY_DATA_SHEET, CERTIFICATE, etc.)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    owl:oneOf _:b73;
    skos:closeMatch gs1:ReferencedFileTypeCode.
_:b73 rdf:first oec:DueDiligenceDocument;
    rdf:rest _:b74.
oec:DueDiligenceDocument a oec:DocumentType;
    rdfs:label "Due Diligence Document"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Documentation of supply chain due diligence processes and risk assessments."@en.
_:b74 rdf:first oec:Certificate;
    rdf:rest _:b75.
oec:Certificate a oec:DocumentType;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityCertificate>;
    rdfs:label "Certificate"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Official certificate from accredited body (ISO, environmental, quality certifications)."@en.
_:b75 rdf:first oec:TestReport;
    rdf:rest _:b76.
oec:TestReport a oec:DocumentType;
    rdfs:label "Test Report"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Technical test results from accredited laboratory or testing facility."@en.
_:b76 rdf:first oec:Manual;
    rdf:rest _:b77.
oec:Manual a oec:DocumentType;
    rdfs:label "Manual"@en;
    rdfs:comment "User manual, installation guide, or maintenance documentation."@en.
_:b77 rdf:first oec:DeclarationOfConformity;
    rdf:rest _:b78.
oec:DeclarationOfConformity a oec:DocumentType;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#EUDeclarationOfConformity>;
    rdfs:label "Declaration of Conformity"@en;
    rdfs:comment "EU Declaration of Conformity stating compliance with applicable EU legislation."@en.
_:b78 rdf:first oec:SafetyDataSheet;
    rdf:rest _:b79.
oec:SafetyDataSheet a oec:DocumentType;
    rdfs:label "Safety Data Sheet"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Safety Data Sheet (SDS) per REACH Regulation providing hazard information."@en.
_:b79 rdf:first oec:EnvironmentalReport;
    rdf:rest _:b80.
oec:EnvironmentalReport a oec:DocumentType;
    rdfs:label "Environmental Report"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Environmental impact assessment, carbon footprint study, or LCA report."@en.
_:b80 rdf:first oec:ThirdPartyVerification;
    rdf:rest rdf:nil.
oec:ThirdPartyVerification a oec:DocumentType;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Review>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ReviewReport>;
    rdfs:label "Third Party Verification"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Independent verification report from accredited third-party auditor."@en.
oec:UnionHarmonisationLegislation a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation>, oec:RegulationTypeCode;
    rdfs:label "Union Harmonisation Legislation"@en;
    rdfs:comment "EU legal act harmonising the conditions for the marketing of products, against which conformity is declared (e.g. the ESPR itself, a delegated act, the Battery Regulation)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2008/768(1)>;
    skos:note "New Legislative Framework concept (Decision 768/2008/EC); every EU declaration of conformity cites the harmonisation legislation it answers. CCCEV's cccev:ReferenceFramework is the SEMICeu generalisation covering any legislation or standard a requirement derives from; this class is the harmonisation-legislation specialisation."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#UnionHarmonisationLegislation>;
    skos:broadMatch <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/ReferenceFramework>, schema:Legislation.
oec:assignedELI a owl:DatatypeProperty;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#LegalResource>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#assignedELI>;
    rdfs:label "Assigned ELI"@en;
    rdfs:comment "European Legislation Identifier (ELI) of the legal act, as an HTTP URI on eur-lex (e.g. https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/ontology>;
    skos:note "The ELI ontology models legal resources as eli:LegalResource nodes; this property carries the identifier as a plain URI reference, which is the shape passports exchange. Property-to-class, so referenced by rdfs:seeAlso rather than a graded mapping."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#assignedELI>;
    skos:broadMatch schema:legislationIdentifier;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI;
    rdfs:domain oec:UnionHarmonisationLegislation.
oec:HarmonisedStandard a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#HarmonisedStandard>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#usedForPresumptionOfConformity>;
    rdfs:label "Harmonised Standard"@en;
    rdfs:comment "European standard adopted on the basis of a Commission standardisation request whose application confers presumption of conformity (Regulation (EU) 1025/2012 Art. 2(1)(c))."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2012/1025>;
    skos:note "ESPR Chapter IX: applying a cited harmonised standard gives presumption of conformity with the covered requirements. Distinct from oec:Certificate (an attestation about one product) and from the legislation itself."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#HarmonisedStandard>;
    skos:broadMatch <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/ReferenceFramework>.
oec:CommonSpecification a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso oec:HarmonisedStandard, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#CommonSpecification>;
    rdfs:label "Common Specification"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Technical specification adopted by Commission implementing act as a fallback route to presumption of conformity where no adequate harmonised standard exists (ESPR Art. 41)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781>;
    skos:note "ESPR Art. 41 fallback instrument; same presumption-of-conformity role as a harmonised standard but adopted by the Commission instead of a standardisation body."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#CommonSpecification>;
    skos:broadMatch <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/ReferenceFramework>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#TechnicalSpecification>.
oec:ConformityAssessmentModule a rdfs:Class;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule>, <https://w3id.org/eudpp#allowsConformityAssessmentModule>;
    rdfs:label "Conformity Assessment Module"@en;
    rdfs:comment "Conformity assessment procedure module per Decision 768/2008/EC Annex II, cited by the applicable Union harmonisation legislation (ESPR Art. 4/43 delegated acts choose the module)."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://ref.openepcis.org/extensions/common/core/>;
    dcterms:source <https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/dec/2008/768(1)>;
    skos:note "New Legislative Framework module taxonomy (A through H1). Modelled like oec:ImpactIndicatorType: a class whose individuals form the controlled list. No GS1, SEMICeu, or schema.org equivalent."@en;
    skos:exactMatch <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ConformityAssessmentModule>.
oec:ModuleA a oec:ConformityAssessmentModule;
